<%# ** ONE SUGGESTION, AS A CHIP THAT FILLS THE BLANKS (two-shapes spec §5). ** Local: `suggestion`.

    §5: "Suggestions as chips above step 1 when the category has any; clicking one fills every blank
    (Stimulus, values carried as data attributes — the server still validates); the chip reads
    '✓ Using this' while the blanks match it."

    ** THE SENTENCE IS THE PANEL'S OWN, RENDERED BY THE PANEL'S OWN PARTIAL. ** A chip is a headline
    and a detail line, which is exactly what `budget_page/_suggestion_<kind>` is — so the copy is not
    written twice and a chip cannot come to describe a measurement differently from the row on the
    Budget page that sent the user here. What differs is only what the control DOES: on that page it
    is a link to this form, and on this form it is the form filling itself in.

    ** THE VALUES RIDE AS `data-prefill-*` AND THE SERVER STILL VALIDATES. ** Every key is one of
    `BudgetsController::BUDGET_FIELDS`, in the unit the form's own controls are in — the engine
    measures per-period money and the amount box holds per-period money on both rate shapes since
    the read-back divides (fix round 1's ruling) — so filling a blank from a chip is the same act as
    typing what the panel just said. Nothing is written: the user still presses the button, and the
    preview re-renders from the server in between.

    ** A CHIP WITH NOTHING TO FILL HAS NO BUTTON, DELIBERATELY. ** A dead-rule suggestion's payload
    is the rule's own id and nothing else — the panel refuses to decide between keeping and deleting
    (`_suggestion_dead_rule`), and there is no figure it could put in a blank. Its sentence is why the
    user is on this form; the decision stays theirs. %>
<%# ** EVERY VALUE IS A STRING BEFORE IT REACHES `data:`, AND THAT IS NOT TIDINESS (measured). **
    `TagBuilder#prefix_tag_option` JSON-encodes anything that is not a String, a Symbol or a
    BigDecimal — so a `Date` arrived in the attribute as `"2026-09-06"` WITH ITS QUOTES, and setting
    a date input to that string is setting it to nothing: the Due field stayed empty on every chip
    click, and the chip then read "Use this" for ever because its own value could never match the
    blank it had just failed to fill. `#to_s` is the same rendering the form's own inputs carry. %>
<%# ** AND THE AMOUNT IS RENDERED AS MONEY, NOT AS A `BigDecimal#to_s` (fix wave — Task 5's minor).
    ** `122.0` is what `to_s` gives, so clicking a chip filled the box with a figure no user would
    type and none of this app's other controls hold — the edit form's own box opens at `"120.0"`'s
    two-decimal twin and the panel's sentence beside the chip says `$122.00`. Two decimals is what
    the input's `step: 0.01` is for and what the sentence promised. `to_d` first, because the value
    may already be a string by the time a caller hands it over. %>
<% prefill = suggestion.prefill[:budget].to_h.transform_values(&:to_s) %>
<% prefill[:amount] = format("%.2f", prefill[:amount].to_d) if prefill[:amount].present? %>
<%= tag.article class: "rounded border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 px-4 py-3 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start sm:justify-between gap-3",
                data: prefill.transform_keys { |field| :"prefill_#{field}" }
                        .merge(chip: suggestion_key(suggestion)) do %>
  <div class="text-sm text-gray-700 space-y-1">
    <%= render "budget_page/suggestion_#{suggestion.kind}", suggestion: suggestion %>
  </div>

  <% if prefill.any? %>
    <div class="shrink-0">
      <%# FULL WIDTH AT 375 (mobile pass, 2026-09-06). Under the chip's own two sentences an 88px
          button reads as a footnote to them rather than the thing that fills the form in, and it is
          the one control on the card.
          THE TWO LABELS ARE THE SERVER'S, on the button, exactly as the entry form's submit carries
          both of its own: the controller chooses between two strings this app wrote rather than
          composing a third in JavaScript. `type="button"`, because a chip must never submit the
          form it is filling in. %>
      <button type="button"
              class="btn btn-secondary w-full whitespace-nowrap sm:w-auto"
              data-action="app--budget--rule-form#useChip"
              data-chip-button
              data-default-label="Use this"
              data-using-label="✓ Using this">Use this</button>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
